# intro(7)

## NAME

intro - introduction to the standard OS

## DESCRIPTION

The standard OS of KiBi Computers is a small Unix-like system. Programs are WebAssembly modules; the commands in `/bin` are written in Zig, and `/bin/lua` runs Lua.

Start with `ls /bin` to see the commands, and `man name` to read about one. `man -k word` searches the page summaries.

## FILES

- `/bin`: commands
- `/sbin`: system programs (init)
- `/etc`: settings
- `/home`: your files (on the hard disk)
- `/tmp`: temporary files in RAM
- `/dev`: devices (`null`, `zero`, `random`, `urandom`, `tty`; attached devices are `/dev/device/<address>`)
- `/usr/share/man`: manual pages

## NOTES

Manual pages are small Markdown files under `/usr/share/man/[LANG/]manN/name.N`. A translation is added by creating a language directory such as `/usr/share/man/fr`; pages without a translation fall back to English.

